  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1,000eb (Very Expensive)<br><strong>Enhances:</strong> Neuroport Cyberdeck Port<br><strong>Option Slots:</strong> 0 (Cyberware Enhancement)</p>\n<p>Neuroport Cyberdeck Port Operating System. The port can now only take a Tetratronic Rippler Cyberdeck, one of which comes with the OS. The Tetratronic Rippler has 4 slots for Hardware and 8 for Programs. Using it for an Overheat or Synapse Burnout Quickhack lets the user try a single DV8 or lower Quickhack on the same target with no Net Action, rolled separately. If either check fails, both Quickhacks fail.</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Every Operating System is incompatible with every other Operating System and with the base cyberware it is for: none of them can be installed while another OS, or that OS's own base cyberware, is anywhere in the user's body or in a worn apparatus they're connected to. The sheet doesn't enforce that.</li></ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Operating Systems &gt; Cyberdeck Port Operating Systems).</em></p>"
